'' A 'const as ustring' READ THROUGH A DESCRIPTOR. StrDescriptorOf_ built the constant's
'' text a NARROW temporary descriptor, while every reader picked its entry point from the
'' constant's USTRING type: 'print G' went to fb_PrintUStr and printed "hi" as the one
'' UTF-16 unit U+6968; ucase, left, mid, a 'byref as const ustring' argument and 'NS.K'
'' the same, and instr answered 0. The constant now gets a ustring temporary
'' (src/mir/lowerstrdesc.tiko). fbc-modern 1.20 has no 'const as ustring' (error 24), so
'' there is no differential; the expected text is the constant itself.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/const-ustring-print.bas -o tests/driver/constustrprint.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/constustrprint.exe
'' RUN: tests/driver/constustrprint.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: hi
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [hi]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: R:hi
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: HI|hi
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ns
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: h|i|i
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  2 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: hi|hi|hi
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
